Package: voiceio
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Hugo Montenegro <h@hugo0.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libportaudio2, ibus, gir1.2-ibus-1.0, python3, python3-gi
Recommends: gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, libnotify-bin, wl-clipboard | xclip
Suggests: ydotool, wtype, xdotool
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://voiceio.dev/
Description: local voice dictation for Linux
 Press a hotkey, speak, and the text appears at your cursor. Speech is
 transcribed on this computer with Whisper; nothing is sent anywhere.
 Streams a live preview into any app through IBus on Wayland and X11.
 .
 This package bundles its own Python and Python libraries in
 /usr/lib/voiceio. The distro's python3 is used only for the IBus engine and
 the tray icon, which need its GObject bindings.
 .
 After installing, run `voiceio setup` as your own user.
